p.src:
For a general density matrix, choose its eigenbasis: $\rho\ket{j}=\lambda_j\ket{j}.$ Insert a complete set of states between $\rho$ and $M$: $\begin{aligned}
\overline{M}
&=\sum_i\bra{i}\rho M\ket{i} \\
&=\sum_{i,j}\bra{i}\rho\ket{j}\bra{j}M\ket{i} \\
&=\sum_{i,j}\lambda_j\delta_{ij}\bra{j}M\ket{i} \\
&=\sum_j\lambda_j\bra{j}M\ket{j}.\end{aligned}$ This is an ordinary weighted average: $\lambda_j$ is the probability of the $j$-th eigenstate, and $\bra{j}M\ket{j}$ is the expectation of $M$ in that state.

