p.src:
Hold $a$ and $a'$ fixed and perform the sum over $b$. The result is a matrix on subsystem $A$: $\boxed{
\rho_A(a,a')
=\sum_b\psi(a,b)\psi^*(a',b)
}.$ This is the reduced density matrix of $A$, or equivalently the partial trace of the pure-state projector over $B$: $\rho_A=\operatorname{Tr}_B\ket{\Psi}\bra{\Psi}.$ The local expectation value becomes $\expect{M_A}
=\sum_{a,a'}\rho_A(a,a')\bra{a'}M_A\ket{a}
=\operatorname{Tr}_A(\rho_A M_A).$

