p.src:
For every local observable, $\expect{M_A}
=\operatorname{Tr}(\rho_A M_A)
=\bra{\phi}M_A\ket{\phi}.$ Subsystem $A$ behaves exactly as a pure state $\ket{\phi}$. For a bipartite pure state, the entropy of $\rho_A$ therefore tests product structure: zero means a product state, while nonzero entropy means entanglement. Values near zero indicate weak entanglement; values near the maximum indicate a state far from any product across this bipartition.

