Take the two-spin singlet $\ket{\Psi^-}
=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}
\left(
\ket{\uparrow\downarrow}
-\ket{\downarrow\uparrow}
\right).$ Its nonzero wave-function components are $\psi(\uparrow,\downarrow)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}},
\qquad
\psi(\downarrow,\uparrow)=-\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}},$ while $\psi(\uparrow,\uparrow)=\psi(\downarrow,\downarrow)=0$.

