p.src:
Now consider $\ket{\Phi}
=\frac12\left(
\ket{\uparrow\uparrow}
+\ket{\uparrow\downarrow}
+\ket{\downarrow\uparrow}
+\ket{\downarrow\downarrow}
\right).$ All four amplitudes equal $1/2$, so normalization follows from four contributions of $1/4$. Tracing over spin $2$ gives $\rho_1
=
\begin{pmatrix}
\frac12&\frac12\\[2pt]
\frac12&\frac12
\end{pmatrix}.$ Its trace is $1$, but $\det\rho_1
=\frac14-\frac14
=0.$

