p.src:
The bra evolves according to $\bra{\phi(t)}
=\bra{\phi(0)}U^\dagger(t),$ so $\begin{aligned}
\braket{\phi(t)}{\psi(t)}
&=\bra{\phi(0)}U^\dagger(t)U(t)\ket{\psi(0)} \\
&=\braket{\phi(0)}{\psi(0)}.\end{aligned}$ Since this equality holds for every pair of initial vectors, $\boxed{U^\dagger(t)U(t)=I}.$

