p.src:
Apply the infinitesimal operator to a state: $\ket{\psi(\epsilon)}
=\left(I-\frac{i\epsilon}{\hbar}H\right)\ket{\psi(0)}
+O(\epsilon^2).$ Subtract the initial state, divide by $\epsilon$, and take the limit: $\frac{\mathrm d}{\mathrm dt}\ket{\psi(t)}
=-\frac{i}{\hbar}H\ket{\psi(t)}.$ Equivalently, $\boxed{
i\hbar\frac{\mathrm d}{\mathrm dt}\ket{\psi(t)}
=H\ket{\psi(t)}
}.$ This is the general Schrödinger equation.

