p.src:
Substitution into the Schrödinger equation gives $\begin{aligned}
i\hbar\frac{\mathrm d f}{\mathrm dt}\ket{\psi(0)}
&=f(t)H\ket{\psi(0)} \\
&=E f(t)\ket{\psi(0)}.\end{aligned}$ Cancel the common vector: $\frac{\mathrm d f}{\mathrm dt}
=-\frac{iE}{\hbar}f(t).$ With $f(0)=1$, $f(t)=e^{-iEt/\hbar},
\qquad
\ket{\psi(t)}=e^{-iEt/\hbar}\ket{\psi(0)}.$

